9. NIC

NIC = Network Interface Card

It allows a computer or device to connect to a network.

It can be:

Ethernet NIC
Wi-Fi NIC

Example:

Computer
   |
   ↓
NIC
   |
   ↓
Network

A NIC normally has a MAC address.

For example:

Laptop
 ├── Wi-Fi NIC
 │      └── MAC: AA:BB:CC:11:22:33
 │
 └── Ethernet NIC
        └── MAC: DD:EE:FF:44:55:66

A device can have multiple NICs, and therefore multiple MAC addresses.

A laptop has both NIC and MAC. They are not the same thing.
LAPTOP
  |
  └── Wi-Fi NIC
        |
        └── MAC Address: AA:BB:CC:11:22:33
NIC = the network interface/hardware in the laptop.
MAC address = the identifier/address associated with that NIC.
